# rules: kotlin-missing-auth
# languages: kotlin
# fixture: kotlin/CWE-306b.kt
# from: CWE-306 Missing Authentication for Critical Function
#
# The rule reports an endpoint in a file that protects some of its others, and
# says nothing about a file that protects none. An application with no
# authentication anywhere has made a decision - the check may live in a filter,
# a gateway or a proxy, or it may be a sample with no accounts at all - and
# reporting every endpoint in it tells the reader nothing they did not know.
# What is a bug is the endpoint that was missed: a guard on three handlers and
# not on the fourth.
#
# The marker for "this file protects something" is a regex, because a Kotlin
# annotation is a modifier on the declaration it precedes: an annotated
# function is a different modifier list and does not match the sink pattern to
# begin with, which is what the exclusion below is really doing.
#
# There is one rule per language for this, and it reports under
# `<language>-missing-auth`. The corpus briefly carried two or three - an
# `-authn` spelling, an `-auth` spelling and this one - written against
# CWE-287, CWE-306 and CWE-862 but all asking the same question: is there an
# authentication guard on this endpoint. They fired on the same lines and a
# route with no middleware got three findings under three ids. Whether the
# missing guard is called authentication or authorization is not something the
# syntax says, so it is one finding; `<language>-862-rbac` is the separate rule
# for the endpoint that does authenticate and then checks no role.
#
# Kotlin Spring handlers with @GetMapping/@PostMapping etc without
# @PreAuthorize/@Secured/@RequiresPermission allow unauthenticated access.

. as $root
| ($root | scan_regex("*.kt";
    ["@(?:PreAuthorize|Secured|RequiresPermission|RolesAllowed)\\s*\\("])) as $protectedSomewhere
| ( ($root | scan_ast(["*.kt"]; [
      "@GetMapping($$$_) fun $F($$$_) { $BODY }",
      "@PostMapping($$$_) fun $F($$$_) { $BODY }",
      "@PutMapping($$$_) fun $F($$$_) { $BODY }",
      "@DeleteMapping($$$_) fun $F($$$_) { $BODY }",
      "@PatchMapping($$$_) fun $F($$$_) { $BODY }",
      "@RequestMapping($$$_) fun $F($$$_) { $BODY }",
      "@PreAuthorize($$$_) fun $F($$$_) { $BODY }",
      "@Secured($$$_) fun $F($$$_) { $BODY }",
      "@RequiresPermission($$$_) fun $F($$$_) { $BODY }",
      "@RolesAllowed($$$_) fun $F($$$_) { $BODY }"
    ])) as $all
    | ( $all | of(["@GetMapping($$$_) fun $F($$$_) { $BODY }","@PostMapping($$$_) fun $F($$$_) { $BODY }","@PutMapping($$$_) fun $F($$$_) { $BODY }","@DeleteMapping($$$_) fun $F($$$_) { $BODY }","@PatchMapping($$$_) fun $F($$$_) { $BODY }","@RequestMapping($$$_) fun $F($$$_) { $BODY }"])
          | outside($all | of(["@PreAuthorize($$$_) fun $F($$$_) { $BODY }","@Secured($$$_) fun $F($$$_) { $BODY }","@RequiresPermission($$$_) fun $F($$$_) { $BODY }","@RolesAllowed($$$_) fun $F($$$_) { $BODY }"]))
          | in_files_with($protectedSomewhere)
        | finding("kotlin-missing-auth";
            "this endpoint has no authentication annotation and its neighbours "
            + "in this file do; add @PreAuthorize or @RequiresPermission, or say "
            + "why it is deliberately open") ) )
| report
